6. Column-family data model demonstration
create 'DemoCF', 'cf1', 'cf2', 'cf3'

put 'DemoCF', 'row1', 'cf1:q1', 'valueA'
put 'DemoCF', 'row1', 'cf1:q2', 'valueB'
put 'DemoCF', 'row1', 'cf2:q1', 'valueC'
put 'DemoCF', 'row1', 'cf3:qX', 'valueD'

scan 'DemoCF'
describe 'DemoCF'
Explanation:
HBase stores data as {rowkey → columnfamily → qualifier → value}. All columns belonging to the same family are stored together on disk (in the same HFile). Different families are stored in separate files. This enables efficient scans of only the required families.
