14. Consistency levels (ONE / QUORUM / ALL)
-- Create keyspace with RF=3 (for demo use RF=1 on single node)
CREATE KEYSPACE ConsistencyDemo
WITH replication = {'class': 'SimpleStrategy', 'replication_factor': 3};

USE ConsistencyDemo;

CREATE TABLE TestData (
    id text PRIMARY KEY,
    value text
);

-- Write with different consistency
CONSISTENCY ONE;
INSERT INTO TestData (id, value) VALUES ('1', 'one');

CONSISTENCY QUORUM;
INSERT INTO TestData (id, value) VALUES ('2', 'quorum');

CONSISTENCY ALL;
INSERT INTO TestData (id, value) VALUES ('3', 'all');

-- Read with different levels
CONSISTENCY ONE;
SELECT * FROM TestData WHERE id = '1';

CONSISTENCY QUORUM;
SELECT * FROM TestData WHERE id = '2';

CONSISTENCY ALL;
SELECT * FROM TestData WHERE id = '3';
Observation:
ONE → fastest, lowest consistency guarantee.
QUORUM → majority of replicas must acknowledge (stronger consistency).
ALL → all replicas must respond (highest consistency, lowest availability).
